	abstract = {DECT-2020 NR (DECT NR+) represents a paradigm shift in industrial wireless communications as the first non-cellular standard integrated into the IMT-2020 5G framework. Despite its potential for massive IoT and URLLC applications, empirical hardware-level evaluations in representative industrial environments have yet to be conducted. This paper presents a first step towards a physical layer performance characterization of DECT NR+ using pre-commercial evaluation boards interfaced with a real-time RF channel emulator. Following a baseline validation against Additive White Gaussian Noise (AWGN) model, we evaluate system performance across a non-line-of-sight (NLOS) factory profile. While SNR results align with theoretical models, performance in multipath environments suggests that integrating retransmission or diversity mechanisms would further optimize link reliability in dense industrial deployments.},
